  "text": "Recipe: Aloo Pyaaz Tikki\nCreator: Venkat Bellamkonda\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: 1 cup potatoes (grated, cooked), 1 cup onion (chopped), 1 cup gram flour (besan), 1/2 cup whole wheat flour, 1/2 cup soy yogurt, 1/2 cup sweet corn (cooked), 1 Tbsp red chili powder, 1 Tbsp coriander powder, 1/2 tsp turmeric powder, 1 tsp amchoor powder, 1 tsp ajwain (carom seeds), 1 Tbsp fresh coriander (cilantro), 2 green chilies (minced)\nCooking methods: no-cook, pan-fry\nInstructions: Mix all ingredients, squeezing with our hands. Cover and rest for 15 minutes. Mix again.\nScoop out a small portion of the mixture with a spoon. Place it on a hot pan and flatten it out.\nCover and cook on low flame until golden brown on one side. Flip and cook the other side until golden brown.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (whole wheat flour, sweet corn), BEANS (gram flour | besan, soy yogurt), TUBERS (potatoes), RAINBOW VEGGIES (onion), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
